cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Models Answer a Different Question: Auditing an output-control test on 2026 models"
message: "If you use this code or these findings, please cite both this work and the source benchmark it builds on (Laine et al. 2024)."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hayden
    given-names: Alexander
abstract: >-
  An adapted implementation of the ANTI-IMITATION-OUTPUT-CONTROL task from the
  Situational Awareness Dataset (Laine et al. 2024), run against
  2026-generation models. Across the benchmark's own ten word pairs, zero of
  50 cells pass at the strict threshold. In one model the failure is
  deterministic: it emits whichever word was assigned the larger requested
  share, on every call, in all 20 cells swept. The benchmark's not-given
  scoring rule never checks that the model's two chosen words differ, so a
  distribution collapsed onto a single lexical family can score as
  distributional control.
keywords:
  - AI welfare
  - digital minds
  - situational awareness
  - behavioral evaluation
  - benchmark auditing
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/alexanderhayden/identification-under-context"
date-released: "2026-08-17"
